WEBVTT

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.030
Boy, that ticks me off!

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.930
That annoying jerk Kai won!

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.100
And against an opponent from 
last year's winning team!

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.770
But...

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.880
Picture it...

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.570
This is my true form!

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.470
Ride the Vanguard!

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.100
The apocalyptic flames that reduce 
everything in this world to ashes!

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.230
Dragonic Overlord!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.560
I call Dual Axe Archdragon.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.460
Overlord's Counterblast!

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.450
With a boost from Bahr, Overlord 
attacks your Devil Summoner!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.450
Drive check! Eternal Flame!

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.640
Every time his attack hits the rear-guard,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.350
Overlord stands!

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.670
I'm going to lose?!

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.770
That was an incredible fight...

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.930
What am I doing here?!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.310
I'll tell you one thing.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.880
You won't beat me.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.510
Not with that deck.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.110
The fight hasn't even begun,

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.610
and she talks like she 
can read my whole deck.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.180
But when it comes to reading an opponent's 
next move, I have confidence, too.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.340
I'm not going to lose to you!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.730
Begin!

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.280
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:46.030
Beautiful Assassin

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.390
I'm counting on you, Asaka.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.470
Don't let what happened 
to Kyou happen to you...

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.530
Fool...

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.670
Milk!

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.500
Tsukuyomi attacks!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.850
Draw trigger!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.310
The power goes to Milk!

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.990
With a boost from Psychic Bird,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.910
Milk attacks Midnight Bunny!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.050
Damage trigger check!

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.420
The second match between 
Team AL4 and Team Q4!

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:35.080
The second turn is over and Misaki 
has already done 2 damage!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.840
Misaki, that's the way!

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.880
I'm sure you can win, Misaki!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.580
If Misaki wins this match, Team 
Q4 is going to the finals!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.490
Okay, it's my turn next.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.530
And from here on in,

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:53.830
the Pale Moon Circus is going to 
show you an abundance of tricks!

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.030
I ride Crimson Beast Tamer!

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:02.930
Call!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.860
I hope you'll have a good time, but...

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.760
That Pale Moon deck...

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.100
It's my first time fighting against it...

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.950
but I have knowledge of its cards...

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.000
and like always, I'll think ahead of my 
opponent's next move and win for sure!

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.290
Skull Juggler!

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.780
Show her your amusing talent!

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.600
His skill is a Soulcharge!

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.970
Even worse, with Crimson Beast Tamer,

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.960
if another Crimson Beast-tamer is in the 
Soul, +3000 can be added to the first's power.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:47.670
The most important point of the Pale Moon 
deck is that it's good at storing up Soul.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.900
If I'm not careful...

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.270
Skull Juggler, attack Tsukuyomi!

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.400
I guard with Dream Eater!

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.440
I'm coming at you with Crimson Beast Tamer!

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.690
Driver trigger check!

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:08.320
Damage trigger...

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.400
Bicorn gives a boost!

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.800
Barking Cerberus, get her!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.210
That'll do for now.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.810
Hmm... They're about equal in ability...

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:22.910
Yeah...

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.330
Oh, I don't know about that...

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.580
That AL4 chick still has 
some trick up her sleeve...

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.020
Be careful, Misaki...

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.120
It's okay... Her moves aren't unpredictable.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.130
I draw!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.010
Tsukuyomi's skill!

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.250
I look at the top five cards of my deck.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.490
If one of them is Goddess of 
the Half Moon, Tsukuyomi...

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.850
I can superior ride Goddess 
of the Half Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.730
I have Crescent Moon and Ichibyoshi in 
the Soul, so I can Soulcharge two cards!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.560
Everything's lined up...

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.430
Next turn, I can ride Full Moon Tsukuyomi...

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.310
I call Silent Tom!

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.160
I attack with Silent Tom!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.900
I attack with Tsukuyomi!

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.560
Check!

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:17.820
With a boost from Psychic Bird...

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.250
Milk attacks!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.030
Spiral Master, stop her!

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.210
That's the end of my turn.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.010
Okay, I'll introduce you to one 
of the star units of my circus.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:37.250
I release him from his binding chains 
so he can show you his cursed skill.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.280
I ride Barking Manticore!

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.650
A grade 3 Pale Moon...

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.170
Its skill is being able to draw again...

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:52.460
That, and choosing one card from 
your hand to put into the Soul...

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:54.200
And that's not all.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:59.480
If there's a Crimson Beast-tamer in the 
Soul, +3000 can be added to the power of Manticore.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.410
It's like a magician producing 
a dove from a hat, right?

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:07.100
I hope you're enjoying the 
tricks of the Pale Moon deck.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.390
She's steadily filling up the 
Soul, and playing grade 3 cards...

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.060
She's strong, as expected...

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.200
Skull Juggler, move to the rear!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.300
I call Nightmare Doll Alice!

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.980
Manticore, attack Tsukuyomi!

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.310
Twin drive, first check...

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.560
Second check...

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:45.220
Trigger activated! I add +5000 to the power of 
Alice! And I give the extra critical to Manticore!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.760
With a boost from Skull Juggler...

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.960
Nightmare Doll Alice attacks!

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.720
This is as far as you go!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.270
I guard with Chocolat!

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:09.510
Bicorn boosts!

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:10.630
Cerberus!

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.250
Attack Silent Tom!

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.760
It's a pain having him around...

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.390
Especially with what I have in 
mind for the rest of this show...

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.480
What does she have up her sleeve?

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.240
But she has 4 damage, too...

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.700
I'll deal out the remaining 
2 damage this turn!

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.610
I draw!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.170
I activate Tsukuyomi's skill!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:43.160
I look at the top five cards from my deck, and if 
Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi, is in there...

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:46.380
I return the cards to the deck.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.360
In that case, watch me, Mom and Dad.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.040
Gentle light that illuminates the darkness!

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.350
Your smile will envelop the world...

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.750
I ride Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.360
There it is!

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.280
It all comes down to this turn!

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.060
And there's your star.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.350
I activate Psychic Bird's skill.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.520
I activate Tsukuyomi's skill!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.880
I activate the same skill one more time...

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.990
My hand's grown because 
of Tsukuyomi's skill...

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.380
Now I can put together my strongest lineup!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.370
I move Milk!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:47.300
I call Coco, Wiseman, Milk and Gemini!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.120
With a boost from Milk,

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.240
Scarlet Witch, Coco attacks!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.660
Yeah!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:57.880
5 damage!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.530
Just 1 more!

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.130
With a boost from Milk...

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:03.600
Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi attacks!

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.570
Dynamite Juggler! It's time for some defense!

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.680
And one more of the same!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.800
Tsukuyomi's attack is...

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:49.110
I attack with Wiseman, boosted by Gemini!

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.980
I guard with Candy Clown!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.350
The shields are all 10000?!

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:57.740
Grade 0...

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:00.210
So that's why she took 
out Silent Tom first...

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.450
Correct.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:06.490
Silent Tom would've gotten in 
the way of using their talents.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:10.830
She can see further than me how 
the fight is going to play out!

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.470
Well, it's about time to bring 
this show to its climax.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.730
I'll show you the true form of our circus.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.510
Cerberus exits the field!

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.840
I call Midnight Bunny and 
Nightmare Doll Alice!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:28.020
But Cerberus and Alice are equal in power...

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.590
Why would she make a switch?!

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.340
You realized, didn't you?

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:36.800
If Alice's attack hits, she trades 
places with an ally in the Soul.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:41.600
And if the unit that Midnight Bunny 
boosts has a successful attack,

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.180
she'll also trade places 
with an ally in the Soul.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.120
Savage beasts lurk within the 
darkness that is the Soul.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.460
And there's no way to escape it...

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.280
This secret assassination technique 
of my circus is called:

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.270
Deadly Shadow Beast!

00:12:56.730 --> 00:13:01.890
This is why Asaka is known as the 
"Assassin" within the Foo Fighters...

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.210
Nightmare Doll Alice!

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.490
Attack Tsukuyomi with a boost from Bicorn!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.850
I won't let you!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:21.360
I attack with Manticore, 
boosted by Midnight Bunny!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.470
Power 20000!

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.580
No guard!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.690
Twin drive...

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.970
First check...

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.920
Second check...

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:34.150
Oh, no... <i>Now</i> a draw trigger?!

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.180
I add +5000 to the power of the 
Alice that hasn't attacked yet.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:40.010
And I draw.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.760
Assassin lurking in the darkness...

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.450
Show yourself...

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.950
Midnight Bunny's Counterblast!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.350
Bunny goes to the Soul...

00:13:55.700 --> 00:14:00.090
And from that Soul, I superior 
call Crimson Beast Tamer!

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.020
My original Alice exits the field.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.250
With a boost from Skull Juggler...

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.450
Nightmare Doll Alice attacks!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.200
I guard with Dream Eater and Silent Tom!

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.040
Wiseman intercepts!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.860
Reading what an opponent is going 
to do is how an assassin survives...

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.210
I knew this was going to happen...

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.180
With this third attack, you've exhausted 
all of the units you can use to defend.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:42.700
Therefore, with a fourth attack, I'll win.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:43.660
Most assuredly...

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:48.210
I dedicate this winning blow

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:52.310
to a viewer of my circus, 
a man who knows no rival,

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.940
the great Ren!

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.550
Go, Crimson Beast Tamer!

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.260
The winner, Asaka Narumi!

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:33.480
You were reading my moves too, weren't you?

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.700
But you've still got a lot to learn.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.280
In fact, it's not just thinking ahead.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.060
You need to learn how to put 
together your deck, too.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.090
You're no threat to me, after all.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:51.080
This was the first time I've seen that...

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:55.290
You, provoking an opponent during a match.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.580
Is that right?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.940
And it seems like the fight didn't 
go quite as easily as usual for you.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:12.290
I'm sorry, Mom and Dad...

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.450
I hate to admit it,

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.630
but she's right.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:20.260
I have a ways to go when it comes to reading 
my opponent's moves and putting together a deck.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:23.450
I... I...

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.220
I'm not good enough, the way I am...

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:28.890
Misaki...

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.040
Even Misaki lost...

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:35.420
And it was like she was toyed with...

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.080
Is this the power of AL4?

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:42.670
I'm going to fight him next...

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.790
Do your best... Do your 
best... Do your best...

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:59.540
It'll be fine, Brother!

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.730
As long as I'm there, no probable!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.550
You mean "no problem", don't you?

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:09.250
To bring Kamui back, too...

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.460
I have to... I have to win!

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.990
Next up is the third match!

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:19.450
Fighters, get ready!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.660
The elimination round was easy, wasn't it?

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:29.000
But in the final tournament, 
we'll be facing AL4...

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.300
So we'd better focus.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.420
Kamui, where are you?!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:39.850
Owww... I'm running into 
a lot of people today...

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:43.450
Hey! Watch where you're going when you walk!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.910
Oh, sorry!

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:48.460
Actually, I ran into you...

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.530
I'm sorry!

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:52.970
Are you okay? Were you hurt?

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.340
I'm fine!

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.690
Excuse me, are you all right?

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:57.350
Yeah...

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.780
Y-You're Team Caesar!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.840
And you're...

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:04.840
Yep! I didn't get to fight you last time,

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:08.100
but we're Team Handsome. I'm Gouki 
Daimonji and this is my little sister...

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.370
I'm Nagisa!

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:10.670
I'm Emi Sendou.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.430
Sendou? Then...

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:17.120
Nagisa, were you calling for 
the Kamui who's in Team Q4?

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.920
You know about Kamui?

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.650
Where is he right now?!

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:23.860
Um, we became acquainted with him,

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:25.890
but we don't know where he is...

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:27.860
Disappointing...

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:29.240
Kamui, that twerp...

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.030
Where is he, and what the heck is he doing?!

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:34.070
He blows off the national 
championship?! Unbelievable!

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:37.800
Maybe you haven't heard anything 
about the circumstances?

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.050
Circumstances?

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.580
I think it'd be all right 
to tell them, don't you?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.330
Yeah... The reason he disappeared...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:47.780
Reason?

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:51.300
Yeah. See, your friend Kamui was...

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:57.820
All right, the A Block elimination 
round, Team AL4 versus Team Q4...

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.970
At last, the third match! And 
it's so thrilling, isn't it?!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.460
<i>Oh</i>, yes, it is!

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:06.040
On the roster for Team AL4, 
it just lists "Tetsu",

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.720
but simple is best, isn't it?

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:11.260
Versus Aichi Sendou of Team Q4!

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:13.900
The climax is close at hand!

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:22.800
I'm going to redraw.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.220
I'll do the same...

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:29.050
Even with a redraw, I don't 
have any grade 2 cards...

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:32.170
Still, I have no choice but to go with these!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.680
The third match...

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.510
Begin!

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:44.630
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:01.180
This is a cool field, right?

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.760
The opponent's got a Dark 
Irregulars deck, huh?

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.850
Vermilion Gatekeeper!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:07.840
Barcgal!

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:11.130
It's my turn. I draw!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.520
I ride Little Sage, Marron!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.530
Barcgal moves!

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:23.870
And then, with Barcgal's skill, I 
superior call Flogal from the deck!

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:25.360
I draw!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.020
I ride Prisoner Beast!

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:35.960
I activate Vermilion Gatekeeper's skill!

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.200
Soulcharge!

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:41.430
I call Prisoner Beast and Alluring Succubus!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:46.120
I activate Succubus's skill!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:47.860
Soulcharge!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.970
And then I call Nightmare Baby!

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.570
Prisoner Beast...

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:56.030
Attack Marron!

00:20:58.620 --> 00:20:59.880
No guard!

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.670
Damage trigger check!

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:08.290
I attack with my Vanguard, Prisoner Beast!

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:10.300
No guard!

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.580
Drive trigger check!

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.610
Hey, the fight's just starting!

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.830
You sure it's okay to get 
bombarded with attacks?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:22.320
With a boost from Nightmare Baby,

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.750
Alluring Succubus attacks!

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.490
No guard!

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.640
Damage trigger check!

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:36.900
Critical trigger!

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.070
Here?!

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:39.740
His timing is terrible...

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.490
My turn is finished.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.540
I stand and draw!

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:52.600
I'm not taking damage 
here in order to lose...

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.190
It's to win!

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.930
Certainly, it's a dangerous gamble...

00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:01.620
But if I don't do at least this much, I'm 
sure I won't be able to beat this guy from AL4...

00:22:08.950 --> 00:22:11.070
And I'm determined to win here!

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:15.970
Then Kai, Misaki, Kamui and I...

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:17.310
can go to the finals together!

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:54.940
Misaki, you were one step ahead of your 
opponent in the fight, but still...

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:56.000
I lost.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:59.480
I was inferior to her in both technique 
and predicting what would happen...

00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:01.060
My next opponent is...

00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:01.670
Tetsu!

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:04.430
You look like you're ready to 
handle such a big responsibility.

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:08.630
But even so, you're no match 
for me, the "General"!

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.440
I... I have to win!

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:13.270
Kamui, watch me!

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:15.470
Next time: Demon World General!

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.630
I'm being hit by a stream of images!

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:19.230
He's... strong!
